From: Codex
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2: use eight buffers for TI J721E CSI2RX

Large RAW12 frames from the TI CSI2RX driver can strand its DMA queue when
rapid stream restarts exhaust the default four-buffer pool. Use eight buffers
for j721e-csi2rx, matching the validated frame-sized capture configuration.

--- a/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2/gstv4l2object.c
@@ -5343,6 +5343,16 @@
     } else {
         own_min = obj->min_buffers + 1;
     }
+
+    /*
+     * The TI CSI2RX driver can strand its DMA queue when large RAW12 frames
+     * exhaust the default four-buffer pool after stream restarts. Keep enough
+     * buffers queued for frame-sized captures while staying within the
+     * documented eight-buffer limit.
+     */
+    if (0 == strcmp(obj->vcap.driver, "j721e-csi2rx"))
+      own_min = MAX(own_min, 8);
+
     own_min = MAX (own_min, GST_V4L2_MIN_BUFFERS (obj));
 
     /* for the downstream pool, we keep what downstream wants, though ensure
